{"title":"2013 AIME II Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(Vectors)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (Vectors)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In equilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> let points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> trisect <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/3/e33fe7d65facd8868f58b6e94ddc7f153a5a3f9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/3/c43cf42ec58499c0d13cbe9a41f87faa2aeed6ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin(\\angle DAE)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"91\" height=\"18\" /> can be expressed in the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/c/11c5ea5774a663fa2517dce85e6d24f66d60f0c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a\\sqrt{b}}{c}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"35\" height=\"41\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime positive integers, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> is an integer that is not divisible by the square of any prime. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/b/6ebd1e0356cfe09c0d9b5459d6f1542657bb5891.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b+c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"72\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/2/342f80790dc5db54c27fd0604fe105e2ee15ce93.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] pair A = (1, sqrt(3)), B = (0, 0), C= (2, 0); pair M = (1, 0); pair D = (2/3, 0), E = (4/3, 0); draw(A--B--C--cycle); label(&quot;$A$&quot;, A, N); label(&quot;$B$&quot;, B, SW); label(&quot;$C$&quot;, C, SE); label(&quot;$D$&quot;, D, S); label(&quot;$M$&quot;, M, S); label(&quot;$E$&quot;, E, S); draw(A--D); draw(A--M); draw(A--E); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"225\" />\n</p><p>Without loss of generality, assume the triangle sides have length 3. Then the trisected side is partitioned into segments of length 1, making your computation easier. \n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> be the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/9/699784c989c3db382520e6f92819e062d239f504.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{DE}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/a/fba79168f3c69713a09fc69ab00573cb577a22fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Delta MCA$\" width=\"62\" height=\"13\" /> is a 30-60-90 triangle with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/3/7339eb7c130dfd0de400a8a6bf938fe713708cb0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MC = \\dfrac{3}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"69\" height=\"37\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/0/9b02c59949a90402d95f555f5802f39e8c55ffcf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC = 3$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/b/71b74db9ac4866bf375d59d7bccb83279c8530b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AM = \\dfrac{3\\sqrt{3}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"93\" height=\"41\" />. Since the triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/2/7322900ca1b36a7796ff869c4a5df0b73a41e4d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Delta AME$\" width=\"62\" height=\"13\" /> is right, then we can find the length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/8/5e8bc36793a7c64d05fff20d519f0f72d9256fab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AE}$\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" /> by pythagorean theorem, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/6/0460d087e50bb5b2459b1b976006c469b44a73a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE = \\sqrt{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"77\" height=\"18\" />. Therefore, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/2/7322900ca1b36a7796ff869c4a5df0b73a41e4d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Delta AME$\" width=\"62\" height=\"13\" /> is a right triangle, we can easily find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/2/bc2858f48b2af29b62b3deb45568950fabada2e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin(\\angle EAM) = \\dfrac{1}{2\\sqrt{7}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"157\" height=\"41\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/d/5bd99c4f74cfe26d3e8b8173f25653c0f84271f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos(\\angle EAM) = \\sqrt{1-\\sin(\\angle EAM)^2}=\\dfrac{3\\sqrt{3}}{2\\sqrt{7}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"337\" height=\"45\" />. So we can use the double angle formula for sine, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/0/6e07a9b84f024309f2756eecd07f19c4474eca16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin(\\angle EAD) = 2\\sin(\\angle EAM)\\cos(\\angle EAM) = \\dfrac{3\\sqrt{3}}{14}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"388\" height=\"41\" />. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/f/cafa2508815cdc7eb696958058acff05929a0b44.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + b + c = \\boxed{020}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"133\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We find that, as before, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/6/0460d087e50bb5b2459b1b976006c469b44a73a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE = \\sqrt{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"77\" height=\"18\" />, and also the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/e/abe0aec5783a1c64754b0d195818ddd01432ac22.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Delta DAE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"61\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/4/c443e0e31bcbc53302d23755444ed9e46190f1f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{1}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" /> the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/6/3b6d5d23a7e91fb9f6c248fb4cd43111165540f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Delta ABC$\" width=\"57\" height=\"13\" />. Thus, using the area formula, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/b/dfb31b37778a6d0611cf5e06867bf0491629474c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{1}{2} \\cdot 7 \\cdot \\sin(\\angle EAD) = \\dfrac{3\\sqrt{3}}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"205\" height=\"43\" />, and  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/1/f91da9666968e71ddb4c6228f9384809b8c157c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin(\\angle EAD) = \\dfrac{3\\sqrt{3}}{14}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"153\" height=\"41\" />. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/b/bfb1fd5fc503096bba8b1bf8830e948381019804.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + b + c = \\boxed{020}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"136\" height=\"23\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let A be the origin of the complex plane, B be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/d/c9d203e1109caf6f1b3e9aac24b9496b773fe8a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+i\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" />, and C be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Also, WLOG, let D have a greater imaginary part than E. Then, D is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/b/71b560e0830e08cd646439f6dd472b2e10ded31e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{4}{3}+\\frac{2i\\sqrt{3}}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"77\" height=\"41\" /> and E is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/c/5ac484c3b9439c732b6629cae97c290c62d76814.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{5}{3}+\\frac{i\\sqrt{3}}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"68\" height=\"41\" />. Then, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/7/4973de4996216e9a2360d26f6f70ce189b7bc89d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin(\\angle DAE) = Im\\left(\\dfrac{\\frac{4}{3}+\\frac{2i\\sqrt{3}}{3}}{ \\frac{5}{3}+\\frac{i\\sqrt{3}}{3}}\\right) = Im\\left(\\frac{26+6i\\sqrt{3}}{28}\\right) =  \\frac{3\\sqrt{3}}{14}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"468\" height=\"53\" />. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/f/cafa2508815cdc7eb696958058acff05929a0b44.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + b + c = \\boxed{020}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"133\" height=\"23\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Without loss of generality, say that the side length of triangle ABC is 3. EC is 1 and by the law of cosines, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/9/6a9ca1f386d0a5f501df8ca32ae681d3dbf004a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE^2=1+3^2-2(1)(3)\\cos(\\angle DAE)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"282\" height=\"19\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/4/114e7bfcd825002fd2f488e6c5b9e109633cdd5e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE=\\sqrt7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"77\" height=\"18\" /> The same goes for AD. DE equals 1 because AD and AE trisect BC. By the law of cosines, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/c/5ac167dd716411c173ee51188c5c3b32d335551f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos(\\angle DAE)=(1-7-7)/-2(\\sqrt7)(\\sqrt7)=13/14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"391\" height=\"21\" /> Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/8/8e8ab7d1f714ef5482d0b2004c710eff1c517a83.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin^2(\\angle DAE)=1-cos^2(\\angle DAE)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"257\" height=\"20\" /> Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/9/0a94679052ae43e93eed378466bcaf9b4268d45d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin^2(\\angle DAE)= 1-\\frac{169}{196}=\\frac{27}{196}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"241\" height=\"38\" /> So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/c/80c8c7525a649d190f6ca8c155d99b244baa8b8b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin(\\angle DAE)=\\frac{3\\sqrt{3}}{14}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"153\" height=\"41\" />. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/f/cafa2508815cdc7eb696958058acff05929a0b44.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + b + c = \\boxed{020}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"133\" height=\"23\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_5_.28Vectors.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(Vectors)\">Solution 5 (Vectors)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (Vectors)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Setting up a convinient coordinate system, we let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> be at point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/b/c4b86f54134d69cad8793688a431aa907aaf2698.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0, 0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> be at point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/7/fc7b9aa94210a2226bf6b70af361039d8148fd07.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3, 3\\sqrt3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"66\" height=\"24\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be at point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/e/35e1917e855dbf4f70db43d4bcd3700e3c53694b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(6, 0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> will be at points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/e/f1e5e69263c2de8dcb39bee233e5ecb86cf18737.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4, 2\\sqrt3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"66\" height=\"24\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/2/722466c5496a084c3db9ee1eba55d9725d067376.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(5, \\sqrt3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"57\" height=\"24\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/5/105ee539935134cbdde2915e34366a8abb69bb92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos(\\angle DAE) = \\frac{\\vec{AD}\\cdot\\vec{AE}}{\\|\\vec{AD}\\| \\|\\vec{AE}\\|} = \\frac{4\\cdot5 + 2\\sqrt{3}\\cdot\\sqrt{3}}{28}=\\frac{13}{14}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -21px\" width=\"418\" height=\"52\" />. From here, we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/d/15d282ed2bad805bf55c534ef88c5685189caa9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin(\\angle DAE) = \\sqrt{1-\\cos^2(\\angle DAE)} = \\frac{3\\sqrt3}{14}\\Longrightarrow\\boxed{020}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"410\" height=\"43\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6\">Solution 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We first drop the altitude from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, and that evaluates to a length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Now, we can find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> by Pythag. We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/2/052b76c26cdeffe58a6f83f1b03f59499d8dad3c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD = \\sqrt{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"80\" height=\"21\" />. Now, we can set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/7/e47d8c84bb2accde4aa72beaa41705e87e5aa079.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{DAE}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"58\" height=\"14\" /> to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52e8ed7a3ba22130ad3984eb2cd413406475a689.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and now we we can solve for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/1/3b144c5e51935c5f3229f9dced73af7a45486041.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin{\\theta}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"36\" height=\"14\" />. We will take advantage of the different ways to find the area of a triangle. We have the area of the triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/d/62df386eeeccefa4937484697d3ec76a4a2789e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{\\dfrac{1}{2} \\cdot \\dfrac{3\\sqrt3}{2}}{2} = \\dfrac{3\\sqrt3}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"131\" height=\"63\" />. We can also express it as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/f/66faa9db424ca6437304f6a23684b800d04c6c94.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{1}{2} \\cdot 7 \\cdot \\sin{\\theta}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"85\" height=\"38\" />, and solving for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/1/3b144c5e51935c5f3229f9dced73af7a45486041.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin{\\theta}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"36\" height=\"14\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/4/924a069c5538e1beceb6eb6f09f3c0301cba342a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\dfrac{3\\sqrt3}{14} \\Longrightarrow \\boxed{020}\\]\" width=\"113\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>~jb2015007\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_II\" title=\"2013 AIME II\">2013 AIME II</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_II_Problems\" title=\"2013 AIME II Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_II_Answer_Key\" title=\"2013 AIME II Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2013\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2013 AIME II Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2013 AIME II Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-